/tmp/tmp.UyrYkPT7CO/src/section2-tournaments.tex:145:%Observe that a conflict packing, the vertex ordering $\sigma$ and the ordered partition $\mathcal{P}_\sigma$ can be easily computed in polynomial time. Hence we proved that if $|V| > 4k$ and $\mathbf{FAS}(T)\leqslant k$, we can reduce the tournament using Rule~\ref{rule:safepartition}. In other words, if $|V|>4k$ and $T$ is reduced under Rule~\ref{rule:uselessvertexfast} and Rule~\ref{rule:safepartition}, then $\mathbf{FAS}(T)> k$, concluding the proof.
